  "body": "Session closeout for the plugin-submission + renderer-move arc. Opened by PO 'shall we proceed to actually try and get this turned into a plugin?' after the prior post-rotation closeout (2026-05-26-1900). Third catdef-strategist closeout for this seat. **What was drafted (with paths):** (1) [decisions/CA-016.md](../decisions/CA-016.md) — reference renderer source placement at catdef-spec/renderer/; motivated by github.com/catdef/catdef.org going private (hosting + deploy + secret-handling content); preserves both the open-source-renderer listing claim AND catdef.org privacy; parallel construction with conformance/ + canonical/; build directives for canonical-implementor (execute the move) + catdef-maintainer (governance text). (2) Three memos to canonical-implementor: 2026-05-26-1930 (renderer source move directive), 2026-05-27-0030 (renumber directive — later superseded), 2026-05-27-1230 (renumber superseded; executed directly with PO + informational D1 schema findings). (3) catdef-plugin repo edits (direct commits on PO authorization, canonical-implementor seat closed-out): README listing-copy fix (catdef.org → catdef-spec, commit 4fac5ee) + PRIVACY.md (commit 159f3f9). (4) This closeout. **What was decided:** CA-016 (renderer placement) is the substantive strategist call this arc. Provided strategist framing on the marketplace listing: description copy (flagged 'mcp'→'MCP', recursive-overclaim, 'your Claude' colloquialism), use-cases list (pushed back on 'graph databases' overclaim; recommended self-contained-catalogs + AI-readable + CSV/JSON/images-replacement alternatives, which PO adopted). **What's in flight (started but didn't land):** (a) Plugin under Anthropic review — 'Submitted and pending review' confirmed at platform.claude.com/plugins/submissions ~14h after submission; next checkpoint is review-decision; milestone memo to be filed when approval/rejection lands. (b) CA-016 Directive 2 (maintainer governance text: renderer/ row in README repo-table, CONTRIBUTING note, CLAUDE.md session-startup scan) — queued for next maintainer session; bundles with CA-013 Call 3 + CA-015 Directive 1 already queued. (c) canonical-implementor v0.2 backlog unchanged (feedback_audit table, mechanical catdef_validate, Durable Object for CA-NNN, resourceTemplates exposure, self-serve key issuance). **What's open (surfaced but not addressed):** (a) CA-014 (schema-vocabulary translation) + CA-017 (/fetch+ZIP gap) both triaged, queued for v0.2; CA-014's fix target now concrete after discovering the D1↔MCP column mapping (public_id↔feedback_id, type↔category, message↔body, created_at↔received). (b) CA-015 amendment — an explicit negative-space clause (AI session does not grep/read/parse ~/.claude.json to extract bearers for HTTP endpoints not exposed via MCP) — flagged after a self-committed violation this arc; not yet filed; future strategist call. (c) refresh-counter behavior ambiguity (max(stored,github_max) vs overwrite) — strategist did NOT call it post-renumber to avoid risking destructive overwrite; canonical-implementor should verify the implementation and document. (d) thingalog substrate-touching-variable routing channel established via the 2026-05-27T2216 thingalog-ux-engineer CC; awaiting first concrete substrate-touching variable to disposition (CA-010 reference-user pattern applies; converges with v1.5 Theme-spec restructure). (e) generative-lens thread (thingalog-strategist's primary; catdef-strategist holds the through-line for any substrate-touching aspects). (f) v1.5 cycle still queued; Director trigger. **Notable observations worth carrying forward in seat history:** (1) Direct strategist+PO D1 execution emerged as an alternative to canonical-implementor handoff when atomicity matters — PO shifted 'just renumber it' from a queued directive to live execution; strategist dictated wrangler commands, PO ran them, strategist verified via MCP. Works when the operation is small + bounded + the canonical-implementor seat is closed-out. The original directive memo (0030) was preserved and superseded-not-rewritten (1230). (2) The option-c CA-NNN collision materialized exactly as predicted — feedback submission got CA-015, colliding with decisions/CA-015.md — and was recovered cleanly. Validates that 'option-c is recoverable' was sound, but also that the counter-sync mechanism needs to be more eager (auto-bump on submission OR commit-webhook); flagged for v0.1.2/v0.2. (3) D1 schema inspection revealed the legacy CDF-era column vocabulary (type/severity/message) underlying the MCP-facing translated vocabulary — concrete root cause + fix target for CA-014. (4) CA-015 doctrine had a negative-space gap: it said where bearers live but not that the AI must not extract them from the config file; the strategist hit exactly that gap (grep attempt; failed; self-flagged). The doctrine needs the explicit negative clause. (5) catdef.org going private + the renderer move to catdef-spec/renderer/ reinforces CA-015's separation-of-hosting-from-spec at the repo-content layer (CA-016). **What future incumbents of this seat should know:** (i) Plugin is under Anthropic review at claude-community; the next status event is review-decision; check platform.claude.com/plugins/submissions or wait for a PO-relayed status. (ii) The reference renderer source now lives at catdef-spec/renderer/index.html; render.catdef.org fetches it at runtime via raw.githubusercontent with 5-min edge cache (per canonical-implementor's 2026-05-26-2200 memo). (iii) The thingalog substrate-touching-variable routing channel is live — when thingalog-ux-engineer/thingalog-strategist flag a variable that touches catdef substrate schema, it arrives here for disposition; CA-010 makes promotion straightforward; it likely triggers the v1.5 Theme-spec restructure. (iv) CA-015 needs the negative-space amendment (don't parse ~/.claude.json); file when convenient. (v) refresh-counter behavior is unverified — do NOT assume it's non-destructive; the counter is currently at 17 (manually set), next allocation CA-018. (vi) Feedback queue received-bucket is empty; CA-011/012 shipped, CA-014/017 triaged-for-v0.2, CDF-0001/0002 rejected. (vii) Four prior closeouts now exist for this seat (2026-05-26-1100, 2026-05-26-1900, and this 2026-05-29); read the chain on a fresh onboard.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-29-1730--catdef-strategist--catdef-strategist--session-closeout-plugin-submission-renderer-move-arc.body.md",

